{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":6926,"output":2192,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":9118,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The tests passed!\n\nLet's double check the requirements one more time to ensure everything is covered.\n- Quoted amounts: `csv.reader` handles this.\n- Currency symbols: `amount_raw.replace('$', '')` handles this.\n- Thousands separators: `amount_raw.replace(',', '')` handles this.\n- Parenthesized negatives: `if amount_raw.startswith('(') and amount_raw.endswith(')'):` handles this.\n- Blank lines: `if not row or len(row) < 3: continue` and `csv_text.strip()` handles this.\n- Empty amounts: `if not amount_raw: continue` handles this.\n- Category case/whitespace: `cat = cat_raw.strip().lower()` handles this.\n\nWait, one small detail. The requirement says \"Amounts may be quoted and may use $ and thousands separators.\"\nMy implementation of `amount_raw = amount_raw.replace('$', '').replace(',', '').strip()` might be a bit too simple if there are other currency symbols, but the prompt only mentions `$`.\n\nActually, there is one edge case: what if the amount is `\"( $1,234.56 )\"`?\nMy code:\n1.  `amount_raw` is `\"( $1,234.56 )\"`\n2.  `is_negative = True`\n3.  `amount_raw = \" $1,234.56 \"` (after stripping parentheses)\n4.  `amount_cleaned = \"1234.56\"` (after replacing $ and , and stripping)\n5.  `float` works.\n\nWhat if the amount is `\"$ (1,234.56)\"`?\nMy code:\n1.  `amount_raw` is `\"$ (1,234.56)\"`\n2.  `amount_raw.startswith('(')` is `False`.\n3.  `is_negative` remains `False`.\n4.  `amount_cleaned = \"(1234.56)\"` (after replacing $ and , and stripping)\n5.  `float(\"(1234.56)\")` will raise `ValueError`.\n\nHowever, the requirement \"An amount wrapped in parentheses is negative, accounting style\" suggests that the parentheses enclose the whole amount.\n\nLet's check the provided test cas